      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:4e64216e62bab250",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "sight",
        "needs": [
          "your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your eyes, so it is not fully a driving lesson. You will want your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down. You can listen to everything else now — leave the section called Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Write बहुत (bahut) from memory: ब, ह, ु underneath the ह, then त."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कब",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कब (kab) — \"when\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit कदा (kadā), \"when\". Look at the first letter and you have the whole point of this lesson: every Hindi asking word starts with क."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have been collecting them without being told they were a set: kyā, kaun, kahā̃, kaise — what, who, where, how — and now कब (kab), when. Five of them, every one written with a क at the front, all doing the same job."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That letter is the signal. Hear a क at the front of a short word at the head of somebody's sentence and you are being asked something, before you have worked out what."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कब (kab) sits where the answer would sit, not at the front of the sentence the way an English question word does: गाड़ी कब (kab) है?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four, and the fifth member of a family you already had."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kyā, kaun, kahā̃, kaise, kab",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kyā, kaun, kahā̃, kaise, kab*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gāṛī kab hai?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gāṛī kab hai?*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "कब (kab), two letters and nothing else",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: कब, two letters and nothing else]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does कब (kab) mean? (\"when\".) What letter do the asking words share?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HI-C71-why",
      "sequence": 2800,
      "title": "क्यों (kyoṁ) — why, and क्योंकि, because",
      "headword": "क्यों",
      "romanization": "kyoṁ",
      "gloss": "why (and क्योंकि, because)",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
