      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:33ac504e14b09aba",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Name the four words of this chapter so far."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: क्यों",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क्यों (kyoṁ) — \"why\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The sixth of the asking words, and it opens on the same क as the other five. The spelling stacks क on य with the vowel-killer, then puts ों on the end: the ो matra and the dot that sends the vowel through the nose."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now the piece that makes it useful twice over. Add कि and you get क्योंकि (kyoṁki) — \"because\". कि on its own is the little word that means \"that\", and क्योंकि is literally \"why-that\": the question turned round to face the answer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So one shape gives you both halves of a reason."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आप क्यों (kyoṁ) नहीं आए? asks it, and any answer that opens on क्योंकि is giving the reason back. You will fill in what follows as your words grow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: आज (āj), भी (bhī), बहुत (bahut), कब (kab), क्यों (kyoṁ). Six asking words in all, and the way to answer the last of them."
            }
          ]
        },
